@startuml connection-setup
title US-02: Connection Setup - Authenticated WebSocket Handshake with Scope

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API\n(ws library)" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nuser_workspaces" as TSDB

Operator -> Dashboard : opens live map

note over Dashboard
  Dashboard holds the Sentinel JWT
  in memory from the Google OAuth
  flow (US-15 workspace-restore).
end note

Dashboard -> API : HTTP GET /stream?token=<JWT>\nUpgrade: websocket

note over API
  Express HTTP server and ws library
  share the same port.
  No separate WebSocket server process.
  JWT is validated before the upgrade
  is accepted - unauthenticated requests
  receive 401 and are dropped.
end note

API -> TSDB : SELECT scope FROM user_workspaces\nWHERE user_id = $1

note over TSDB
  Scope is loaded once at connection time
  and held in the in-memory connection map.
  No database lookup on every pushed message.
end note

TSDB --> API : { geo_region, entity_types, alert_types }

API --> Dashboard : 101 Switching Protocols\n(WebSocket handshake complete)

note over Dashboard
  Connection is persistent.
  Dashboard does not poll.
  Server pushes position updates and alerts
  filtered by the operator's saved scope.
end note

Dashboard --> Operator : map rendered, scoped live stream active

== On disconnect ==

Dashboard -> Dashboard : detect connection drop
Dashboard -> API : reconnect with same JWT\nGET /stream?token=<JWT>
API --> Dashboard : 101 Switching Protocols\nscope reloaded from user_workspaces
Dashboard --> Operator : live updates resume

@enduml
